(1)  202/    155C :                     ; the Nemesis decompressor uses prefix-free codes (no valid code is a prefix of a longer code)
(1)  203/    155C :                     ; e.g. if 10 is a valid 2-bit code, 110 is a valid 3-bit code but 100 isn't
(1)  204/    155C :                     ; also, when the actual compressed data is processed the high bit of each code is in bit position 7
(1)  205/    155C :                     ; so the code needs to be bit-shifted appropriately over here before being used as a code table index
(1)  206/    155C :                     ; additionally, the code needs multiple entries in the table because no masking is done during compressed data processing
(1)  207/    155C :                     ; so if 11000 is a valid code then all indices of the form 11000XXX need to have the same entry
(1)  208/    155C :                     NemBCT_ShortCode:
